From 496baef8f4c386a8828adb2de86fc442c9d3ce37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "a.tzitanov" <alexypoloz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 15:51:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(search): observation distillation + relevance gating
 in agent loop
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Between tool_execution and the next reasoning step, large observations
(> distill_min_chars) pass through a new distill_observation activity:
one LLM call compresses them to query-relevant facts and grades
relevance (relevant/partial/irrelevant). This:

- bounds reasoning-context growth on large corpora (the whole history
  is re-sent each step), preventing silent context-window overflow;
- gates the accumulator CRAG-style — clearly irrelevant results no
  longer pollute the synthesizer context.

Full NodeWithScore sources still feed synthesize_answer unchanged, so
distillation trims only the agent's working memory, not answer detail.
A hard observation_max_chars cap backstops history size even when
distillation is off. Knobs (distill_enabled/min_chars/max_chars) are
resolved from AgentSettings at submit time and propagated via
SearchParams so the workflow never reads env at runtime (replay-safe).

Verified against litellm → ollama gemma4:e4b: 8155-char observation
compacted to 57 chars (key fact retained) on-topic; graded irrelevant
off-topic.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
